(4716868, 678784, 66515, '<td valign="top">Okay...I have to say. Where is the dappled light? I see some sort of light in the top left but its not dappled at all.</td>', 'Okay...I have to say. Where is the dappled light? I see some sort of light in the top left but its not dappled at all.', '2008-05-22 02:51:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716869, 680607, 66515, '<td valign="top">Your model could have taken up more of the frame and had she been placed IN the light I think this would have been a more interesting shot. The way it is right now its a picture of a barn interior with a girl in it.</td>', 'Your model could have taken up more of the frame and had she been placed IN the light I think this would have been a more interesting shot. The way it is right now its a picture of a barn interior with a girl in it.', '2008-05-22 02:52:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716876, 680493, 66515, '<td valign="top">I won''t take marks off but why did you feel it was necessary to include "dappling" in the title? What would you have called this shot had it been for a free study? That, in my opinion is the approach you should take to titling your image for challenges. If you have to use the challenge topic in the title then it usually means you are trying to shoe horn your image into the challenge. (Not in this case however)<br/> <br/>Now that my mini-rant is over how about something constructive? Good demonstration of dappled light that certainly fits the challenge. I like the monochrome but I am also curious what this would look like in colour. Dappled light tends to make a shot feel warm and relaxed. Monochrome tends to "sanitize" an image for lack of a better term. Just a thought though and I think it could work either way.<br/> <br/>I really like the leading lines of the shot. Its too bad that the back stones are so bright but it probably couldn''t be helped. <br/> <br/>Overall a good entry for the challenge. Well done!</td>', 'I won''t take marks off but why did you feel it was necessary to include "dappling" in the title? What would you have called this shot had it been for a free study? That, in my opinion is the approach you should take to titling your image for challenges. If you have to use the challenge topic in the title then it usually means you are trying to shoe horn your image into the challenge. (Not in this case however) Now that my mini-rant is over how about something constructive? Good demonstration of dappled light that certainly fits the challenge. I like the monochrome but I am also curious what this would look like in colour. Dappled light tends to make a shot feel warm and relaxed. Monochrome tends to "sanitize" an image for lack of a better term. Just a thought though and I think it could work either way. I really like the leading lines of the shot. Its too bad that the back stones are so bright but it probably couldn''t be helped.  Overall a good entry for the challenge. Well done!', '2008-05-22 02:58:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716880, 680382, 66515, '<td valign="top">Not really seeing the dappled light I am afraid. The subject is in deep shadows and you have a really bright sky so my eye is all over the place. Leaving your model right where she is and taking your shot from the tree to the right likely would have captured better lighting. (I am guessing though)</td>', 'Not really seeing the dappled light I am afraid. The subject is in deep shadows and you have a really bright sky so my eye is all over the place. Leaving your model right where she is and taking your shot from the tree to the right likely would have captured better lighting. (I am guessing though)', '2008-05-22 03:01:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716892, 680460, 66515, '<td valign="top">Great image but make sure you use the full size allowed (640 px) in this case. Generally speaking, the bigger the image the better the impact. <br/> <br/>I don''t generally like colored borderds but it works well here. (Keep in mind that the site puts a small black border around anyways that might not work with the border you''ve already put on)<br/> <br/>I like the colors you captured and the soft background really is pleasing.<br/> <br/>I like the subtlety of the light here and naturally it suits the challenge well.</td>', 'Great image but make sure you use the full size allowed (640 px) in this case. Generally speaking, the bigger the image the better the impact.  I don''t generally like colored borderds but it works well here. (Keep in mind that the site puts a small black border around anyways that might not work with the border you''ve already put on) I like the colors you captured and the soft background really is pleasing. I like the subtlety of the light here and naturally it suits the challenge well.', '2008-05-22 03:04:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716961, 679627, 5746, '<td valign="top">I hope it''s not the direction for scores? Seriously: I like warm tones here. The sign makes the story. The viewer has to ask the question: "Why?" and try to answer it. I like such pictures a lot.</td>', 'I hope it''s not the direction for scores? Seriously: I like warm tones here. The sign makes the story. The viewer has to ask the question: "Why?" and try to answer it. I like such pictures a lot.', '2008-05-22 04:15:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716968, 680493, 5746, '<td valign="top">It looks like the fence is pretty close. However, I think you could make this picture lifting camera a bit higher to include more graves in frame and crop out the grass in the lower part. It would give more interesting perspective. Nice dappled light. Maybe more contrast would make it more aparent.</td>', 'It looks like the fence is pretty close. However, I think you could make this picture lifting camera a bit higher to include more graves in frame and crop out the grass in the lower part. It would give more interesting perspective. Nice dappled light. Maybe more contrast would make it more aparent.', '2008-05-22 04:30:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716971, 680621, 5746, '<td valign="top">I like reflections on the wall. The sky is clear and intensive blue, but I would crop it more, as it is not very interesting. In fact the lowest part of the building (with reflections) is the most interesting one. I would''e create nice abstract picture.</td>', 'I like reflections on the wall. The sky is clear and intensive blue, but I would crop it more, as it is not very interesting. In fact the lowest part of the building (with reflections) is the most interesting one. I would''e create nice abstract picture.', '2008-05-22 04:37:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716972, 680272, 5746, '<td valign="top">Very nice composition. Soft colours, nice detail. I like the way the viewer has to imagine her eyes behind shades. Nice, soft and natural portrait. No unnecessary posing. Very appropriate for a young, beautiful girl.</td>', 'Very nice composition. Soft colours, nice detail. I like the way the viewer has to imagine her eyes behind shades. Nice, soft and natural portrait. No unnecessary posing. Very appropriate for a young, beautiful girl.', '2008-05-22 04:40:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716975, 680319, 5746, '<td valign="top">Picture looks a bit blury and flat. Higher f number and more saturation would make the leaves stand out. You could also find a nice branch and focus on it. Now there is no main subject in the picture.</td>', 'Picture looks a bit blury and flat. Higher f number and more saturation would make the leaves stand out. You could also find a nice branch and focus on it. Now there is no main subject in the picture.', '2008-05-22 04:55:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716976, 679994, 5746, '<td valign="top">Picture taken from above her eyes makes her face a bit long. Maybe if you tried to make it on her eye level it will bring back proportions. I think there is to much of hat visible, which competes with her face. Nice dappled light and beautiful golden eye.</td>', 'Picture taken from above her eyes makes her face a bit long. Maybe if you tried to make it on her eye level it will bring back proportions. I think there is to much of hat visible, which competes with her face. Nice dappled light and beautiful golden eye.', '2008-05-22 04:57:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716977, 680362, 5746, '<td valign="top">The flowers which you focused on are a bit overexposed. Probably mid day light, which is harsh on plants. I think it would''ve been better to focus on the remaining flowers and try early morning or evening light. Also the part of flower on the right competes with your main subject. Cropping it out would help IMHO.</td>', 'The flowers which you focused on are a bit overexposed. Probably mid day light, which is harsh on plants. I think it would''ve been better to focus on the remaining flowers and try early morning or evening light. Also the part of flower on the right competes with your main subject. Cropping it out would help IMHO.', '2008-05-22 05:15:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716979, 679259, 5746, '<td valign="top">The part which is in focus is very small comaring to the rest of the picture. The eye is searching for the main subject finding the blured edge than finally landing on the lower left corner, where you focused. Dappled light is well visible. Maybe more centered composition or bigger DOF could help.</td>', 'The part which is in focus is very small comaring to the rest of the picture. The eye is searching for the main subject finding the blured edge than finally landing on the lower left corner, where you focused. Dappled light is well visible. Maybe more centered composition or bigger DOF could help.', '2008-05-22 05:18:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716986, 679664, 5746, '<td valign="top">Nice detail. The light is limited making the picture a bit dark, but it adds to the mood. Background however is not very attractive. I would try to blur it more.</td>', 'Nice detail. The light is limited making the picture a bit dark, but it adds to the mood. Background however is not very attractive. I would try to blur it more.', '2008-05-22 05:23:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(4716987, 679551, 5746, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shade of blue. Probably you tried to focus on the petals, but it''s a pity the leaves lost detail. Maybe a bit of fill light would enhance the photo.</td>', 'Beautiful shade of blue. Probably you tried to focus on the petals, but it''s a pity the leaves lost detail. Maybe a bit of fill light would enhance the photo.', '2008-05-22 05:25:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(4717008, 680475, 66635, '<td valign="top">Spectacular!  I love this!</td>', 'Spectacular!  I love this!', '2008-05-22 05:39:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(4717009, 678784, 66635, '<td valign="top">Nice picture, but IK''m not seeing any dappled light.  Am I missing something here?</td>', 'Nice picture, but IK''m not seeing any dappled light.  Am I missing something here?', '2008-05-22 05:40:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(4717053, 679928, 5746, '<td valign="top">Dappled light is there, however there is no composition in it :( Maybe if you made a close up at the object or show a bit more of surroundings it would''ve help.</td>', 'Dappled light is there, however there is no composition in it :( Maybe if you made a close up at the object or show a bit more of surroundings it would''ve help.', '2008-05-22 07:06:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4717054, 679081, 5746, '<td valign="top">The roots are great. Sky is barely visible, so I would suggest to crop it out and focus on the roots. It would''ve been interesting to move a bit to the right to get different persective and give the picture more air by getting rid of the heavy tree on the left or making it less prominent.</td>', 'The roots are great. Sky is barely visible, so I would suggest to crop it out and focus on the roots. It would''ve been interesting to move a bit to the right to get different persective and give the picture more air by getting rid of the heavy tree on the left or making it less prominent.', '2008-05-22 07:08:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(4717105, 680537, 91405, '<td valign="top">love it, hope to find it on the front page next week!!</td>', 'love it, hope to find it on the front page next week!!', '2008-05-22 08:57:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(4717109, 680176, 18073, '<td valign="top">Sorry but this doesn''t quite work for me.  I think its the lack of a focal point that I find off putting.  This might not be so bad if there was a repeating pattern in the image, but this isn''t the case either.</td>', 'Sorry but this doesn''t quite work for me.  I think its the lack of a focal point that I find off putting.  This might not be so bad if there was a repeating pattern in the image, but this isn''t the case either.', '2008-05-22 09:03:39.000000', NULL, 1),
