(4729410, 679158, 65234, '<td valign="top">Looking at this result you''ve got a respectable final score, pretty normal distribution of votes in the ever-popular Bell curve pattern, and some nice comments telling you what people like and what they don''t.  There are always low votes, even on the best entries, and about a billion threads from people trying to understand them.  My advice is to not bother trying to understand ;-)<br/> <br/>And while I didn''t vote on this one, I would have given it a 7 or so.  Great color, interesting patterns and a creative approach that made dappled light instead of finding a subject affected by natural dappled light.  Were it my image I would hue-shift the orange to blue/purple and center the object; it is almost centered now which always invites people to notice it''s slightly off, and the orange interrupts the otherwise fairly symmetrical look of the background.<br/> <br/>My 2 or 3 cents ;-)</td>', 'Looking at this result you''ve got a respectable final score, pretty normal distribution of votes in the ever-popular Bell curve pattern, and some nice comments telling you what people like and what they don''t.  There are always low votes, even on the best entries, and about a billion threads from people trying to understand them.  My advice is to not bother trying to understand ;-) And while I didn''t vote on this one, I would have given it a 7 or so.  Great color, interesting patterns and a creative approach that made dappled light instead of finding a subject affected by natural dappled light.  Were it my image I would hue-shift the orange to blue/purple and center the object; it is almost centered now which always invites people to notice it''s slightly off, and the orange interrupts the otherwise fairly symmetrical look of the background. My 2 or 3 cents ;-)', '2008-05-28 09:14:13.000000', NULL, 0),
