(4754502, 679524, 91197, '<td valign="top">Usually the pics I vote high don'' t do high scores! This one got a 9 from me. And each time I see it gives me feelings. So I ll pick it as a favorite!</td>', 'Usually the pics I vote high don'' t do high scores! This one got a 9 from me. And each time I see it gives me feelings. So I ll pick it as a favorite!', '2008-06-06 16:31:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4754958, 680380, 39850, '<td valign="top">Every time I see this image, I keep wondering - <i>is</i> this an orchid bud?<br/> <br/>edit: Thank you for the clarification.  The folds on the edge of the petals and the way they are tucked in there, plus your unique angle made this, yes, very mysterious.  A very unique image.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-07 09:39:01.</i></td>', 'Every time I see this image, I keep wondering - is this an orchid bud? edit: Thank you for the clarification.  The folds on the edge of the petals and the way they are tucked in there, plus your unique angle made this, yes, very mysterious.  A very unique image.', '2008-06-06 22:24:29.000000', '2008-06-07 10:39:01.000000', 0),
(4755323, 680380, 32084, '<td valign="top">For those that are wondering and have asked - this is a Oriental Lily (Lilium) Monan Lisa flower preparing to open.  Hopefully I won''t ruin it for anyone, but this was shot in the studio.  For Mother''s Day all the great flowers were gone and all we could find were these - all still closed up.  It took over a week for them to open and when they began to do so they were amazing.  As others have mentioned, it almost looked like something from a scary movie.  So, I drug one down to the studio, along with several tubs of these branch things that the wife has all over the place.  I call them booby-traps as they grab me wherever I go.  One set of these branch things are behind the lilly and one set are in front and off to the right side.  I then shot my 580EX II (off camera) through the front set of branches to get the dappled light. A reflector was also used on the left to fill in the shadow area a little.  Thanks for all of the comments.</td>', 'For those that are wondering and have asked - this is a Oriental Lily (Lilium) Monan Lisa flower preparing to open.  Hopefully I won''t ruin it for anyone, but this was shot in the studio.  For Mother''s Day all the great flowers were gone and all we could find were these - all still closed up.  It took over a week for them to open and when they began to do so they were amazing.  As others have mentioned, it almost looked like something from a scary movie.  So, I drug one down to the studio, along with several tubs of these branch things that the wife has all over the place.  I call them booby-traps as they grab me wherever I go.  One set of these branch things are behind the lilly and one set are in front and off to the right side.  I then shot my 580EX II (off camera) through the front set of branches to get the dappled light. A reflector was also used on the left to fill in the shadow area a little.  Thanks for all of the comments.', '2008-06-07 03:03:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4768181, 680537, 12611, '<td valign="top">Really nice shadows, just a great feathery look. I like the placement of the top branch as well.</td>', 'Really nice shadows, just a great feathery look. I like the placement of the top branch as well.', '2008-06-14 00:57:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4778940, 680537, 35720, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot Shez, great abstract image!</td>', 'Wonderful shot Shez, great abstract image!', '2008-06-21 06:59:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4790386, 679445, 72579, '<td valign="top">THAT''S ME!!!!!!!!!!</td>', 'THAT''S ME!!!!!!!!!!', '2008-06-29 19:54:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4794800, 680478, 70265, '<td valign="top">I have the same 18-200, and it''s a wonderful lens ... ! I''m thinking maybe a faster shutter speed and/or slightly higher aperture might have helped your focus here. Also, check the focus settings in your camera menu, and make sure VR is turned on, on your lens. (I only turn it off for tripod shots). I''ve also experimented w/manual focus, which you turn on on your lens ... especially for macro-type shots. I apologize in advance if you already know all this!</td>', 'I have the same 18-200, and it''s a wonderful lens ... ! I''m thinking maybe a faster shutter speed and/or slightly higher aperture might have helped your focus here. Also, check the focus settings in your camera menu, and make sure VR is turned on, on your lens. (I only turn it off for tripod shots). I''ve also experimented w/manual focus, which you turn on on your lens ... especially for macro-type shots. I apologize in advance if you already know all this!', '2008-07-01 14:55:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4823504, 679416, 91131, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all the nice comments - both of these boys are called Oriental Shorthairs.  They are very intelligent, friendly and extremely people oriented - my favorite breed.</td>', 'Thank you for all the nice comments - both of these boys are called Oriental Shorthairs.  They are very intelligent, friendly and extremely people oriented - my favorite breed.', '2008-07-14 07:25:15.000000', NULL, 0),
